      translation: "Certainly were there in Yusuf and his brothers signs for those who ask, [such as] When they said, \"Yusuf and his brother are more beloved to our father than we, while we are a clan. Indeed, our father is in clear error. Kill Yusuf or cast him out to [another] land; the countenance [i.e., attention] of your father will [then] be only for you, and you will be after that a righteous people.\" Said a speaker among them, \"Do not kill Yusuf but throw him into the bottom of the well; some travelers will pick him up - if you would do [something].\"",
